  Quote of the Week:

  Pope Julius II, in reply to Michelangelo, who had asked which of his 
artistic tools the Pope would like to try (1506):
  "Nay, give me a sword, for I am no scholar."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:

  Winter gave way to spring.  Haggis Wen Yen prepared his armies to defend 
Yablonovyy and the surrounding provinces.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Haggis Wen Yen for this year.


  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  Hector (#180) has arrived in Dzhugdzhur from Kamchatka.


  Here is the financial report for Haggis Wen Yen's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 0 gold in revenue.  0 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  0 gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Haggis Wen Yen was 
left with 7 gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Lucan
To: Haggis Wen Yen

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season I prepared to quench my thirst for 
glory.  I prepared my forces to defend Shelekhov Gulf and the surrounding 
provinces.

  Thy humble servant,   Lucan


